# Conformance probe pack for sequential constructs inside one another (spec
# 0.8), most significant bit first. Public. No kinds.
#
#   byte 0      n
#   byte 1      presence p.1 and p.2, then 6 unused bits
#   byte 2      the number of items
#   each item   three presence bits q.1 to q.3 of its own, then
#                 q.1   qty in 5 bits
#                 q.2   a chain: x in 7 bits and the extension bit; y in 7
#                       bits and an extension bit written 0
#                 p.1   val in 8 bits: a presence of the message, named
#                       inside the item, so every item holds val or none does
#               then zero bits to the next whole byte
#   p.2         an 8-bit length in bytes, then nums: before each item one bit,
#               1 = an item follows; an item is val in 7 bits
format     conformance-seq-nested
version    0.8.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
field   probe.n  8  uint
presence p 2
pad 6
group   probe.items count 8
  presence q 3
  if q.1
    field  probe.qty  5  uint
  end
  if q.2
    chain
      field  probe.x  7  uint
      fx
      field  probe.y  7  uint
      fx
    end
  end
  if p.1
    field  probe.val  8  uint
  end
  align 8
end
if p.2
  length 8
    group  probe.nums while
      field  probe.val  7  uint
    end
  end
end
